      "snippet": "Mar 23, 2016 · When reading an object, we check its expiration timestamp, and if it's in the past, we return nothing, and delete the object while we're at it. But the problem is that if a key is never touched, it just takes up memory for no reason. So Redis adds a second layer of random active expiration.",
